2026-09-20 13:25:33,375 DEBUG   anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'headers': {}, 'timeout': {'connect': 5.0, 'read': 600, 'write': 600, 'pool': 600}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-235c5e8b-c7b3-41e3-a397-979ff8a89ef7', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 1024, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '## Available skills\n\n\n- classify: Use this skill when the Worker agent receives a "classify" subtask, typically downstream of an Expert summary or directly from the Planner for bounded-decision tasks. Assigns input to a fixed label set, then dispatches the label-mapped action via the MCP server. Worker is the only agent in the chain that produces a real side effect. Triggered by: subtask.type == "classify", or any task requiring a categorical decision followed by an action.\n\n- summarize: Use this skill when the Expert agent receives a "summarize" subtask from the Planner. Compresses raw/verbose input (task output, retrieved documents, prior agent chatter) into a structured summary with a confidence signal, and decides whether the result is safe to pass downstream or needs to bounce back to the Planner for re-scoping. Triggered by: subtask.type == "summarize", or any input routed to the Expert agent.\n\n\n## User request\n\nTicket #420: Customers report the checkout page returns a 500 error when applying a discount code larger than 20%. Started after yesterday\'s deploy of the pricing-service. Affects roughly 15% of checkout attempts. Support has received 8 complaints in the last hour. Please summarize this ticket and classify its priority.\n\n\n\nProduce the plan now as the JSON object described in the system prompt.'}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-5', 'system': 'You are the Planner agent. Break the user\'s request into an ordered list of\nsteps. Each step is dispatched to exactly one available skill — only use\nskill names from the "Available skills" list you are given; never invent one.\n\nFor a step whose skill is "summarize", `input` must include:\n  - source_text (string): the raw text to summarize\n\nFor a step whose skill is "classify", `input` must include:\n  - content (string, or an object with summary/key_points): the material to classify\n  - label_set (optional array of strings): omit to use the skill\'s default labels\n\nRespond with ONLY a single JSON object, no markdown fences, no prose:\n{\n  "plan": [\n    {"step_id": "<short unique id>", "skill": "<skill name>", "input": { ... }}\n  ]\n}\n\nEvery step_id must be unique within the plan. The plan must contain at least\none step.\n'}}
