2026-09-20 20:06:33,204 DEBUG   agents.skills.client: run_skill: raw_response='I\'ll help you classify this issue. Let me first read the SKILL.md file to understand the exact output format and requirements.\nLet me try a different approach:\nNow I\'ll analyze the content and classify it according to the criteria:\n\n**Analysis of the issue:**\n- **500 error** on discount codes >20% (application failure)\n- **Root cause identified**: pricing-service deploy yesterday (recent change)\n- **15% impact**: affects checkout attempts (significant business impact)\n- **8 customer complaints in last hour**: active customer-facing issue\n- **Severity indicators**: System error (500), quantified business impact (15%), active user complaints\n\n**Classification rationale:**\nThis is a **"critical"** issue because:\n1. It\'s a complete system error (HTTP 500), not degraded performance\n2. It affects production checkout functionality (revenue-generating process)\n3. It has measurable business impact (15% of checkout attempts)\n4. There are active customer complaints (8 in last hour)\n5. Root cause is recent (deploy yesterday), suggesting rollback may be needed\n\nThis meets the definition of a critical severity issue requiring immediate attention.\n\n```json\n{\n  "label": "critical",\n  "confidence": 0.95,\n  "fallback_used": false\n}\n```'
