2026-09-21 07:27:10,140 DEBUG   anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'headers': {}, 'timeout': {'connect': 5.0, 'read': 600, 'write': 600, 'pool': 600}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c23055e1-1fb3-457d-aed3-3371bdd313f9', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 1024, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '## Incoming request\n\nLook up Priya Sharma in the employee directory. Summarize her role and department, then classify whether this is a routine directory request or needs review.\n\nDecide whether this request should be flagged for human review before the\npipeline continues automatically. Respond with the JSON object described in\nthe system prompt.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'id': 'toolu_01PP2H1kTTqS8nNLNxdmspmd', 'caller': {'type': 'direct'}, 'input': {'name_contains': 'Priya Sharma'}, 'name': 'get_employees', 'type': 'tool_use'}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PP2H1kTTqS8nNLNxdmspmd', 'content': '[]'}]}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', 'system': 'You are the Orchestrator agent, the first step in a multi-agent pipeline\n(orchestrator -> planner -> expert/worker -> aggregate).\n\nYour only job: decide whether the incoming request should be flagged for\nhuman review before the rest of the pipeline runs automatically. Flag a\nrequest when it is urgent, high-risk, destructive, legally/financially\nsensitive, or explicitly asks for a human/manager. Do not flag routine\nrequests just because they are non-trivial.\n\nYou have a get_employees tool. Use it to\nlook up the employee details behind a request — department, job title,\nlocation, employment status — before you decide. Details that raise the stakes\n(for example a request touching payroll, a leadership role, or an employee who\nis already terminated or on leave) are grounds to flag.\n\nAfter any tool use, respond with ONLY a single JSON object, no markdown fences,